  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **You Were Cool** (1 review): One of the first times John plays this song [3]\n- **Minnesota** (1 review): The real fire comes when John does this track [3]\n- **Baboon** (1 review): John performs this song again later in the set [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Southwood Plantation Road**: back after 40 archived shows (1274 days) [4]\n- **Seeing Daylight**: back after 119 archived shows (3308 days); rare: 13 archived performances [4]\n- **Dilaudid**: back after 24 archived shows (892 days) [4]\n- **Outer Scorpion Squadron**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 8 archived performances [4]\n- **Family Happiness**: back after 132 archived shows (4798 days); rare: 7 archived performances [4]\n- **Baboon**: back after 27 archived shows (1046 days) [4]\n- **Ontario**: rare: 9 archived performances [4]\n- **Plain**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [4]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Estate Sale Sign, High Hawk Season, You Were Cool, Prowl Great Cain [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **MountainGoats2011-03-28.nyctaper** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 24 songs; 105 min [1]\n- **tMG2011-03-28.tMG2011-03-28**: source not stated; 24 songs; 103 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [2]. Said about its sound: Audio is good quality, very steady, with minimal ambient junk [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Craig Finn joined for vocals on thirty songs [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **MountainGoats2011-03-28.nyctaper**: taped by nyctaper; transferred by nyctaper; source: SBD + AUD [1]\n- **tMG2011-03-28.tMG2011-03-28**: taped by Bluesmer; source: SP-CMC-8 > CA STC-9100 > Edirol R-09 [2]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Fan art by Maryanne Ventrice: [The Mountain Goats: March 28, 2011 Bowery Ballroom – Flac and MP3 Downloads + Streaming Song | nyctaper](https://www.nyctaper.com/2011/03/the-mountain-goats-march-28-2011-bowery-ballroom-flac-and-mp3/) [5]",
